    "text": "One morning, Alex woke up to the sound of his own footsteps echoing in the empty room. He checked the clock—7:00 AM—and felt a strange sense of disorientation. Everything was familiar, but there was no real world around him. He tried to reach for his phone, only to find it missing. As he wandered the room, he noticed that the walls were lined with screens and buttons, and the air was filled with the hum of a distant video game engine. He realized he was not in his own home but in a virtual world, a game he had never played before.\n\n*** \n\nAlex spent the next few days exploring the game, trying to figure out how he got here. He discovered that he could move around, interact with objects, and even speak to other players. But as he delved deeper, he began to notice strange inconsistencies—his memories were fragmented, and the game seemed to change without warning. One day, he found himself in a vast, open world where he could see the sky and the stars, but the rules of the game were unclear. He was determined to find a way out, but the more he explored, the more he felt like he was losing himself in a simulation.",
